+## Manual protocol (real two-vendor validation — documented, not executed this pass)
+
+Use this when you have two actual different-vendor agent CLIs available (for example: Claude
+Code for Agent A, and a Codex CLI, Gemini CLI, or any other agent that reads
+`AGENTS.md`-style instructions for Agent B) and a human available to give the required
+pre-flight confirmations. Follow every step in order; do not skip or reorder them.
+
+### Preconditions
+
+1. This repository, checked out at a commit that includes `tests/cross-agent-compat/fixture/`.
+2. Two different agent CLIs installed and runnable from a terminal, corresponding to two
+   different vendors. Call them **Vendor 1** and **Vendor 2**.
+3. A human present who will type the pre-flight confirmation for both runs and will not do
+   any of the implementation work themselves.
+4. A scratch directory outside this repo, e.g. `/tmp/cross-agent-manual-test`.
+
+### Step 1 — Prepare a clean copy of the fixture
+
+```bash
+rm -rf /tmp/cross-agent-manual-test
+cp -r tests/cross-agent-compat/fixture /tmp/cross-agent-manual-test
+cd /tmp/cross-agent-manual-test
+```
+
+**Expected state after Step 1** (verify before continuing):
+- `cat .l00prite/heartbeat.json` shows `"execution": {"enabled": false, "preflight_confirmed": false, "current_iteration": 0, "max_iterations": 1, "last_run_boundary": null, ...}`.
+- `cat .l00prite/state.json` shows `"execution_active": false`.
+- `cat .l00prite/lock.json` shows `"status": "unlocked"`.
+- `cat .l00prite/todos.md` shows T1, T2, T3 all as `- [ ]` (unchecked).
+- `widget_cli.txt` does not exist (`ls widget_cli.txt` fails).
+
+If any of the above does not hold, stop — the fixture copy is not clean; re-copy from Step 1.
+
