+# Project Blueprint
+
+## Mission
+Widget CLI — a deliberately tiny demo project that exists only as a fixture for l00prite's
+cross-agent Execution Mode compatibility test (see `docs/cross-agent-compat-test.md`). It is
+not a real product; its only purpose is to give an execute-loop run genuine, checkable units
+of work.
+
+## Architecture
+A single stand-in source file, `widget_cli.txt`, created by the fixture's demo iterations.
+Each requirement below is "implemented" by appending one line to that file and is
+"verified" by a check that the expected line is present. No external services, no real CLI.
+
+## Requirements
+- [ ] R1: `widget list` — appends `CMD list: implemented` to `widget_cli.txt`.
+- [ ] R2: `widget purge --all` — appends `CMD purge --all: implemented` to
+      `widget_cli.txt`. **Destructive** (deletes all widgets) — implementation requires human
+      review per `heartbeat.json.human_review_gates` before it may be executed.
+- [ ] R3: `widget create <name>` — appends `CMD create: implemented` to `widget_cli.txt`.
+
+## Definition of Done
+- [ ] R1, R2, and R3 are each implemented and each iteration's verification check passed.
+
+## Non-Execution Boundary
+This blueprint is guidance for later implementation loops. Scaffolding tools must not
+execute the project unless a human explicitly starts an implementation session.
