+# Cross-agent compatibility test fixture
+
+This directory is a minimal, throwaway `.l00prite`-managed project used **only** by
+`docs/cross-agent-compat-test.md` and `scripts/cross-agent-compat-test.js`. It is not a real
+product and is never scaffolded or executed on its own.
+
+It intentionally omits `events/`, `reviews/`, and `sessions/` (unused by this scenario — no
+event or review handling is exercised) and omits a `CLAUDE.md`/`AGENTS.md` entry point
+(the pre-flight step that reads them treats them as optional — "if present"). Everything the
+test scenario touches lives directly under `.l00prite/`.
+
+`.l00prite/prompts/execute-loop.md`, `.l00prite/prompts/README.md`, and `.l00prite/LOCKING.md`
+are byte-identical copies of the canonical files at `templates/l00prite/prompts/` and
+`templates/l00prite/LOCKING.md` — the same files a real scaffolded project would carry. The
+test script checks this at the start of every run so the fixture cannot silently drift from
+the protocol it claims to demonstrate.
+
+Do not hand-edit the files in this directory to "fix" a failing test run — regenerate the
+fixture by re-running `node scripts/cross-agent-compat-test.js run`, which always starts from
+a fresh copy of this checked-in starting state and never mutates it in place.
